{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective","id":913049,"title":"Beast detective","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-12T15:54:42-07:00","id":913049,"title":"Beast detective","content":"So I'm a bit inspired on idea of beast detective that is feed by the solving enigmas ( or something connected to teaching lessons from them, maybe by saying 'full story' to his clients? ) and looking for new Chambers or supernatural family members in his cases. It really vague now and will be glad for your advice on it. <b>What Family and Hunger could have this beast?</b> <b>What could be it's Horror?</b><br /> <br /> In long term, I want to cross it's paths with my mages detective PCs in London game, but would rather write it rather general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T16:43:39-07:00","id":913079,"title":"","content":"Depending on the <i>why</i> of the mystery chasing, I could see this Beast being a Nemesis (&quot;I will drag you out into the light!&quot;) or a Collector (&quot;You secrets are mine now.&quot;), perhaps a Predator (&quot;The game is afoot, Watson!&quot;).<br /> <br /> Any Family could work, really, though I'd favor Ugallu. <br /> <br /> \u2022The Anakim detective is unstoppable. he shrugs off bullets and legbreakers in equal measure, pushes through lies and misdirection like fog, and just won't <b>quit!</b><br /> <br /> \u2022The Eshmaki moves through the shadows, unseen and unheard. When all the pieces come together he strikes with unnerving swiftness.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Makara is a deceptively beautiful creature. There soft voice and shining eyes lure you into spilling you guts... until that lovely being drags you into a undertow of your own making and drowns you in your sin.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Namtaru is a wretched creature, a scraggly, poor drunk who you normally would never be caught dead with. But they can go places you never would, and know how to turn their untouchable status to their advantage.<br /> <br /> \u2022The Ugallu sees all, knows all. No matter where you run they find you, and soon everyone else will know everything about you.<br /> <br /> Not sure about the Horror or Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T17:45:00-07:00","id":913110,"title":"","content":"I call dibs on writing a sheet for this detective.<br /> <br /> I already have some characteristics in mind, but I have to ask a few questions to see which will be included.<br /> <br /> 1) Do you want him/her to establish Kinship with the PCs?<br /> <br /> 2) Will he/she be a recurring NPC? If so, will his/her goals line up with or go against those of the PCs?<br /> <br /> 3) How powerful do you want him/her to be in loose terms?<br /> <br /> 4) What are the blind spots in the skill set of the PCs, both magic and mundane? <br /> <br /> 5) What sort of Mysteries do the PCs usually investigate?<br /> <br /> 6) What is the Consilium's official stance on co-operating with other supernaturals?<br /> <br /> 7) How much do the PCs know about Beasts?<br /> <br /> Sorry if that's complicated. I want to make sure this NPC will be both general and specific enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T23:19:22-07:00","id":913260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913079#post913079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the <i>why</i> of the mystery chasing, I could see this Beast being a Nemesis (&quot;I will drag you out into the light!&quot;) or a Collector (&quot;You secrets are mine now.&quot;), perhaps a Predator (&quot;The game is afoot, Watson!&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I get right that Predator would only need to go on investigations and Nemesis or Collector would need to end their case to fulfill it's Meal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:23:05-07:00","id":913439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913260#post913260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get right that Predator would only need to go on investigations and Nemesis or Collector would need to end their case to fulfill it's Meal?</div> </div> </div> </div> If you mean the Predator could likely feed simply through hunting down his prey, while the Nemesis would actually need to unleash some sort of punishment and the Collector would need to acquire secrets, then yes?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm away from the book right now, so I'd have to check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Clarified 06-13-2016, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:36:50-07:00","id":913454,"title":"","content":"Relevant? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/865489-crossover-concept-detective-agency?p=871936#post871936\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...936#post871936</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T04:07:59-07:00","id":918541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Do you want him/her to establish Kinship with the PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not from the start - but eventually? Yeah.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Will he/she be a recurring NPC? If so, will his/her goals line up with or go against those of the PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would want him to be rather minor recurring character - someone that shows up, from time to time in plot, going in some interactions with PCs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) How powerful do you want him/her to be in loose terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Midly experianced mage like, probably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4) What are the blind spots in the skill set of the PCs, both magic and mundane?</div> </div> </div> </div>This will be tught one, as they are now cabal of Masters or would-be-Masters. But I would say they lack Life magic a lot. On mundane area, I would say that they a bit behind in Social Skills. Our Silver Ladder Acanthus is running P.I. business.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5) What sort of Mysteries do the PCs usually investigate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Main plot is based on possible coming of Hieromagus. Other than this they are drown to Abyssal stuff - they fight with Yellow Sign Intruder, confronted with Cult of Doomsday Cult, battle with Ochema of Void.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6) What is the Consilium's official stance on co-operating with other supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>'We shy from it' - it's not strictly ban, but mages try to stick to their own matters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=913110#post913110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7) How much do the PCs know about Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>For now - nothing. I wanted to introduce them with this NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T08:57:47-07:00","id":919119,"title":"","content":"One thing I'm wondering - there's a mention somewhere in the corebook of a Collector who collects lovers, can a detective Collector &quot;collect&quot; criminals by putting them in jail? Would they need to add the jail as a Chamber first?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now I'm envisioning a particularly creepy interpretation of Batman as a Collector, with Arkham as his &quot;collection&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":582,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","user":"Morangias","date":".  Because I'm Batman! 06-22-2016, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T17:17:16-07:00","id":919388,"title":"","content":"Here you go. I can expand on this and give full stats, modifying as needed. If you want to know more, just ask.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Quon Lui is a rather quiet man, and prefers to only say what he believes must be said. He is polite to a fault, often giving firm handshakes and a confident smile. His physique appears unremarkable at first, but he has quite a bit of muscle for someone of his size. His hair and goatee are cut professionally short, and his face has scholarly gauntness to it.<br /> <br /> Being the son of two successful lawyers, Quon always had a fascination for the truth, and the various ways people find to change and hide it. He earned his parents fortune and started working as a lawyer himself early. Even though he was respected by his peers, he always felt that there more layers to the lies and truths of the world than most people dared investigate. This made him rather paranoid and gave him recurring nightmares.<br /> <br /> In these dreadful visions, he would hear the thundering footsteps of something massive, but when he turned around, the creature would be gone, leaving behind houses and buildings that were torn open. Some people were taken away, while others were reduced to bloody smears by giant fists, and anything of value was ripped from any bindings and stolen. People rebuilt and sometimes found those who were kidnapped, but could never catch the monster.<br /> <br /> One night, after a particularly stressful day of work, Quon had the same nightmare. But this time, he decided to search for the unseen threat. He ignored the warnings of his parents, and soon saw strange shadows everywhere. He discovered patterns in the way people were taken, and found the giant squatting inside a dark alleyway, holding objects fashioned from the missing people and covered in bloody runes. He dodged around the ogre until he ripped off his necklace, and the last thing he remembers is the tall shadow pulling him into its maw with unbeatable arms.<br /> <br /> When he woke up, Quon knew that monsters were real, and he had become one of them. The blood in his veins ran cold, but his curiosity soared. Where were all these people taken? What became of them? And most important, how could he bring them back and benefit from it?<br /> <br /> Not long after that, Quon gathered his resources and contacts to start his work as a private investigator. He found that he had a new partner who helped get inside places that would have killed him were he still human. This ogre of bone and shadow, covered in bloody runes of a thousand rituals, was his door into a new world. Endless mysteries of both men and magic awaited, and all he had to do to take them all was reach out and rip out the Truth.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So, he's an Anakim Collector. He makes extensive use of Skeleton Key, as the supernatural is often involved in missing people cases in the CoD. He has Kinship with local mages, changelings and a sin-eaters. He focuses on Social and Mental traits, and has a werewolf True Friend called Yuan Chiang who values everyday honesty more than he does, and protects the comparatively frail Quon.<br /> <br /> He feeds his Hunger for Hoard by taking information to solve the cases, with coercion if need be. He would get the most Satiety when he rescues someone from the clutches of a mind-controlling Elder or a clever True Fae. He likes to take whatever magic items he can find in the dark corners of the world and other planes of existence, storing them in his Lair (more specifically, a Chamber that's based on his office and looks like Baba Yaga's hut). His Atavisms would be Needs Must, Eye Of Heaven, Relentless Hunter, From The Shadows and Mimir's Wisdom. Main Nightmares would be We Know All Your Secrets, They Are All Around You and You Will Never Rest. His Life is Scholar, his Legends are Relentless + Watchful and his Lair is 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-24-2016, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T06:29:54-07:00","id":919675,"title":"","content":"Generally? I love him! Great NPC idea. But there is minor thing - must he be Chinese? I run London game, do not think there is large China subculture there, much more Hindu, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:26:20-07:00","id":919905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/913049-beast-detective?p=919675#post919675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally? I love him! Great NPC idea. But there is minor thing - must he be Chinese? I run London game, do not think there is large China subculture there, much more Hindu, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div> He doesn't have to be Chinese, I picked his ethnicity from the most common Asian ones in London. You can change his name into an Indian one without trouble.<br /> <br /> I'd keep his &quot;magic wielding giant&quot; Horror, however. To me, that Horror would look more like a slender troll than a hulking ogre. It would be covered in symbols of occult might instead: a cloak of living snakes coming from its shoulders, a cyclopean eye made of rune-covered stone, goat legs enveloped by fog, that sort of thing. I also imagine the runes in his eye glowing a light green while the rest of his flesh is made of shadow.<br /> <br /> I was wondering how close to a sorcerer type you could get with with a Beast, and it came to me that many Mages are like an Anakim or Ugallu Collector. So I gave Quon Atavisms and Nightmares that are good for gathering information. If you want him to be more combat capable, just give him Limb From Limb and Dragonfire (I imagine the latter manifests as spewing hungry crows, grasshoppers and such). His Horror would have more Power and Finesse than Resistance.<br /> <br /> The Lair resembles a branching cave system (Maze) with only a few cracks and fungi giving a sickly green light (Poor Light). Illusory relics of arcane power (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/649174-a-new-lair-trait\"><b>Wondrous</b></a>) lead the uninvited into cages of stone (Sealed Exits), while the location of the true magic items is known only to Quon. He uses this combination of Lair Traits to trap those involved in the crimes he investigates, promising them freedom and false power in exchange for information, later erasing the memory of the encounter with Tabula Rasa if he wants.<br /> <br /> With this set up and his investigative skills, he has acquired a lot of occult knowledge, which by itself does not satisfy him. Despite his scholarly personality, he likes socializing, mostly with other supernaturals that also have a fascination with the occult. But here's a plot hook: he is getting a desire to show other supernaturals, especially mages, that there are some types of power that cost so much they aren't worth it. This might lead him to develop Tyrant as a second Hunger, and try to join the Guardians Of The Veil, maybe even the Silver Ladder. He might also try to investigate Abyssal phenomena to understand what dangers it represents, and ask for the PCs' help in exchange for rare Artifacts and secrets he has stored away. He can also offer to help the PCs rescue someone lost inside the Invisible Realms/Emanation/Abyssal Verge etc.<br /> <br /> Do you like those storytelling hints? Would you be interested in a full sheet, or just the main traits and dice pools?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-23-2016, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T02:30:02-07:00","id":920261,"title":"","content":"Really great and thought NPC! I would like full stats, as it will be secondary character - and in <b>Mage</b>, more stats you got, better to use NPC. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T14:55:23-07:00","id":920574,"title":"","content":"Here is the full sheet. I worked pretty hard on it, so I hope you like it. The PCs sound pretty advanced, so I went ahead and made Quon pretty advanced too. Feel free to adjust any of his traits. I used some house rules for the Horror. I decided to give him Family Ties with Changelings, Sin-Eaters and Mages because of the following reasons: a lot of disappeared people and objects end up in the Hedge and the Underworld, the Astral is a useful information gathering tool, and all three splats are great for investigation.<br /> <br /> I left his final Chamber slot open so he can have a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/734872-homebrew-idea-new-type-of-family-dinner?p=787169#post787169\"><b>Vein</b></a>, probably for Mana. You can imagine his Horror as being a lot like <a href=\"http://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/darksiders/images/d/d5/Vulg.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20120104024128\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Vulgrim from Darksiders</b></a>, but more Cyclops and Strix-like. In his human form, he dresses more colorfully than the iconic occult detective, preferring bright blue and green. There are no whiskey flasks or cigarette butts lying around in his office, but it has a lot of occult items (without powers) that he likes to explain to customers. This is how he creates Lair Resonance to enter his Hut Of Treasures, which is where he keeps all of his true mystical items. He is often seen eating and offering healthy snacks, which he cooks himself on his free time with the help of Mimir's Wisdom, all the better to use in Social Maneuvering. Please change his True Friend from a werewolf to a Mage who's a member of a Cabal that has worked with the PCs, so as to explain how they met him.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that, while not truly deceitful or too proud to admit his mistakes, Quon is an overachiever and an opportunist with too much curiosity. His experience with the occult and the law have lead him to believe he knows better than certain investigators and vigilantes. This is likely true for low Wisdom mages who want to use magic for revenge, but he tends to assume most mages are low Wisdom, which can make sound him arrogant and even invasive. He considers his options carefully, even when socializing and having fun. He can use Mimir's Wisdom to boost his Politics and offer favors to get pretty much anything, which can also spark conflicts.<br /> <br /> Lair Hints: he uses his version of Dragonfire to selectively destroy electric lights to create Lair Resonance for Poor Light. However, he prefers to direct people into locations and/or social situations where they are trapped somehow, and where he can offer a way out with golden favors, creating Lair Resonance for Wondrous, Maze and Sealed Exits.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Quon Li</b><br /> <b>Legend:</b> Relentless + Watchful<br /> <b>Life:</b> Scholar<br /> <br /> <b>Family:</b> Anakim<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Hoard<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Attributes:</b> Intelligence 4, Wits 4, Resolve 4<br /> <b>Physical Attributes:</b> Strength 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3<br /> <b>Social Attributes:</b> Presence 3, Manipulation 4, Composure 3<br /> <br /> <b>Mental Skills:</b> Academics (Law) 3, Crafts 1, Computer (Background Checks) 1, Medicine 1, Occult (Supernatural Trails) 3, Politics 2, Investigation (Missing People, Body Language) 4, Science 1<br /> <b>Physical Skills:</b> Athletics 2, Brawl 2, Drive 1, Firearms 1, Larceny 0, Stealth 2, Survival (Hedge) 1, Weaponry 1<br /> <b>Social Skills:</b> Animal Ken 0, Empathy (Motivations, Desires) 3, Expression (Bragging) 2, Intimidation (Insinuation) 2, Persuasion (Favors) 4, Socialize 2, Streetwise (Criminals) 2, Subterfuge (Careful Omission) 2<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Two Legends, Area Of Expertise (Body Language, Law), Common Sense, Encyclopedic Knowledge (Academics, Occult), Eye For The Strange, Good Time Management, Interdisciplinary Specialty (Favors, Body Language, Law), Investigative Aid (Investigation, Occult), Patient, Professional Training 3 (Detective: Investigation, Occult, Empathy), Trained Observer 1, Tolerance For Biology, Allies (Police 3, Changelings 2, Sin-Eaters 2), Contacts (Police, Hunters, Changelings, Sin-Eaters), Fame 1 (Police), Fast-Talking 3, Fixer, Pusher, Table Turner, Status (Police 3, Changelings 2, Sin-Eaters 2, Mages 1), Striking Looks 1 (Confident), Resources 3, Martial Arts 2<br /> <br /> <b>Atavisms:</b> Needs Must, Relentless Hunter, Mimir\u2019s Wisdom, Limb From Limb, Dragonfire (Crows &amp; Vermin)<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmares:</b> We Know All Your Secrets, You Are Not Alone, Tabula Rasa, Cursed Object<br /> <br /> <b>Family Ties:</b> Changelings, Sin-Eaters, Mages<br /> <br /> <b>Defense:</b> 5<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed: </b>11<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 7<br /> <b>Health:</b> 8<br /> <b>Lair:</b> 4<br /> <b>Starting Satiety: </b>3<br /> <br /> <b>Horror Traits</b>: Power 6, Finesse 8, Resistance 6, Size 8, Health 11, Defense 6, Initiative 7, Speed 13<br /> <b>Lair Traits:</b> Sealed Exits, Poor Light, Wondrous, Maze<br /> <b>Chambers:</b> Well Of Magic (Heart), Hut Of Treasures, Labyrinth Cave, Dark Streets Of Mysteries</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 06-25-2016, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]